{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages.\n\nBut wait - the puzzle says the award was \"created in the 2000s.\" The Booker Prize was created in 1969. However, the Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005 (2000s). Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, let me re-read the puzzle: \"originally created in the 2000s (the award itself)\". This could mean the award was created in the 2000s. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005. But Obioma's books were shortlisted for the regular Booker Prize, not the International one.\n\nLet me reconsider the puzzle structure. The puzzle might be about a different award. Let me think about the \"preceding year\" clue: Book B won the award in the year Book A was published, but Book B was released the preceding year. \n\nLet me check the Man Booker International Prize winners in the 2010s and see if there's a book translated into 25+ languages that was a contender.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize winners list 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015\", \"International Booker Prize 2016 2017 2018 2019 winner\", \"book translated into 25 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize contender\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d468be68a3fc4c3eadc4230a","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789475061,"id":"chatcmpl-4ec50931-33c6-91e2-bc62-e6220f4e4e1c","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":17654,"completion_tokens":335,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":17989,"cached_tokens":11392,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":11392},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}